================================================================================
Why these files are vendored
================================================================================

The SK-V3 dispatch surface compiles authored .asm primitives (see build.rs)
that depend on x86inc.asm's calling-convention abstractions (`cglobal`, REPX,
xmm/ymm/zmm reservation, AVX-512 ZMM clobber rules) and on x86util.asm's macro
toolbox (PALIGNR, PSHUFLW, transpose helpers).  Vendoring keeps the build
deterministic and avoids a runtime dependency on a system FFmpeg / x264.

